Thank you, Secretary Rubio, for hosting the G20 Foreign Ministers’ Meeting in Atlanta, Georgia this weekend!

Perfect timing for one of the greatest and most storied rivalries in college sports: Georgia-Florida.

In the spirit of Larry Munson’s greatest call…27-8, Dawgs On Top!

@SecRubio 
@GeorgiaFootball

The 2026 IFCPF Cerebral Palsy World Cup kicked off today at the Arthur M. Blank U.S. Soccer National Training Center in Fayette County!

Our U.S. Men’s Cerebral Palsy team defeated Canada, 7-0, in the opening match.

I was honored to greet the players, officials, and supporters who traveled from across the world to our part of Georgia, and I am especially proud of Harris County native Jacob Crumbley, a starter for our national team, for his incredible performance.

I hope this tournament inspires every American with cerebral palsy and the families and caregivers who support them!

@ussoccer 
@ifcpf

Yesterday, I was honored to visit LaGrange College to deliver an initial $1.88 million federal investment in STEM education and workforce development at LaGrange College.  This funding will grow the Manufacturing Engineering Technology degree to prepare students for skills-based careers across our part of Georgia.

Earlier this year, I brought the U.S. Secretary of Education Linda McMahon to our Congressional District to discuss the need for additional investment in workforce development, and I am grateful for her support of LaGrange College’s 21st Century Workforce Readiness Program.

Thank you to Dr. Susanna L. Baxter for your partnership, and thank you to Coach Wes Dodson for inviting me to visit your football team! 

@LaGrangeFTBL 
@LaGrangeCollege 
@CoachWMD 
@usedgov

I am honored to welcome my friend, Small Business Administrator Kelly Loeffler, to Harris County — the 10th visit to our district by a Member of President Trump’s Cabinet over the past two years.

For 13 straight years, Georgia has been the #1 State in the country for business, and I am proud to extend that economic winning streak by passing the largest tax cut in American history, eliminating job-killing regulations, and providing small businesses with quicker access to capital.

As Chairman of the Small Business Subcommittee on Innovation, Entrepreneurship, and Workforce Development, I am grateful for our partnership with Administrator Loeffler, a champion for our state and a leader for our country.

@SBA_Kelly
@SBAgov

Earlier this week, I honored the LaGrange College Panthers on the Floor of the United States House of Representatives for their second consecutive victory in the Clash of Highway 29!

Congratulations to the Panthers, led by Coach Wes Dodson, QB Henry Brodnax, and DB Messiah Scandrett on a 31-7 win against the Point University Skyhawks, continuing their winning streak in Georgia’s newest college football rivalry.

@LaGrangeFTBL 
@PointFootball

I had a wonderful time hosting a Fireside Chat for over 100,000 constituents from President Franklin Delano Roosevelt’s beloved Little White House in Warm Springs this afternoon.  Thank you to everyone who participated!

President Roosevelt ​​pioneered the concept of a “Fireside Chat”, and I was honored to continue that tradition, as I deeply care about preserving the rich history, values, and culture of Georgia’s 3rd Congressional District, especially as we celebrate our Country’s 250th anniversary.

When President Roosevelt left the Yalta Conference he told his aides – who were worried about his ailing health – “If I can just make it back to Warm Springs, I’ll be OK.”

President Franklin Delano Roosevelt left an indelible mark on our Congressional District, and we are proud to have been the home away from home for a President.

@GaStateParks 
@OfficialLWH

Thank you to all who came to our tailgate at the Newnan High School vs. LaGrange High School football game last night!

First played in 1908, the Newnan-LaGrange rivalry is one of the oldest in Georgia high school football, and after last night’s result, the LaGrange Grangers now lead the series, 52-39-5.

It was amazing to hear the stories of some of the former players who played in this rivalry many years before!

@GrangerSports 
@Granger_Nation

I had a wonderful time touring the Biblical History Center in LaGrange this afternoon.  The museum is celebrating its 20-year anniversary this year, and it features large-scale archaeological replicas of Biblical structures, interactive exhibits, and hundreds of artifacts from ancient Israel.  The Biblical History Center offers guests an opportunity to journey to the past and experience what life was like during the time of Jesus and his disciples.

Thank you to the Biblical History Center team for inspiring the next generation of archaeologists and Biblical scholars!

@VisitLaGrange

Today, I was honored to visit the next generation of Georgia’s leaders at Blanchard Elementary School.  As students return to school this month, we’re reminded of the incredible teachers who shape countless lives and the opportunities that a quality education provides.

Thank you to Principal Lester and Blanchard Elementary School for inviting me to visit, and thank you to the amazing educators of the Muscogee County School District for guiding the future of Georgia through your classrooms!

@MCSDSchools

